  'operations.searchKnowledge': {"name":"operations.searchKnowledge","kind":"helper","resource":"operations","purpose":"Search the knowledge base by meaning-bearing text, articles first and assets second, with typo tolerance, ranked hits and verbatim snippets.","inputSchema":{"query":{"name":"query","type":"string","required":true},"opts":{"name":"opts","type":"object","required":false,"fields":[{"name":"scope","type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["articles","assets","companies","users","groups","websites","asset_passwords","password_folders"]},"required":false},{"name":"limit","type":"number","required":false},{"name":"snippetChars","type":"number","required":false},{"name":"company_id","type":"number","required":false},{"name":"updated_since","type":"string","required":false},{"name":"min_score","type":"number","required":false},{"name":"exact_only","type":"boolean","required":false},{"name":"tier","type":"string","enum":["auto","vendor","index"],"required":false},{"name":"refresh","type":"boolean","required":false}]}},"outputSchema":{"type":"KnowledgeSearchResult","drops":[],"dropsUnresolved":false,"fields":[{"name":"hits","type":"array","items":{"type":"object"},"required":true},{"name":"meta","type":"object","typeName":"KnowledgeSearchMeta","resolved":true,"required":true}],"fullType":"KnowledgeSearchResult","expand":"expand: true returns the full typed record"},"examples":["await hudu.operations.searchKnowledge('example', { scope: [], limit: 1, snippetChars: 1, company_id: 1, /* ... */ })"],"effect":"read","flags":[],"dryRun":false,"permissions":"unknown","pagination":{"mode":"none","defaultPageSize":null,"maxPageSize":null,"nonPaginated":true},"resolution":{"basis":"client-scan","maxScanRecords":20000,"maxScanPages":100},"retry":{"retryableStatuses":[429,500,502,503,504],"backoff":"exponential","baseDelayMs":200,"maxDelayMs":30000,"jitter":"up-to-25%-of-delay","idempotencySupport":"none"},"errors":["BAD_REQUEST","CONFIG_ERROR","NETWORK_ERROR","RATE_LIMIT","UNAUTHORIZED"],"related":["articles.search","assets.search","operations.searchAcrossResources"],"preferredWhen":"Preferred over articles.search, assets.search or any resource list whenever the caller is looking for CONTENT rather than an exact field: a phrase in an article body, a mistyped title, a serial or a custom-field value. Use the exact-match helper tier instead when the caller already holds an id, a slug or a domain.","usage":"Mode-selecting helper with ONE entry point. mode:\"search\" (the default) needs query and returns ranked hits with plain-text snippets, scores and the follow-up call; it defaults to tier \"index\" when called as the MCP tool (the SDK default stays lazy). mode:\"help\" returns how to use the tool. mode:\"resources\" returns the searchable-resource table derived from the plan rows that declare a search vendor filter. A field the selected mode cannot honour throws CONFIG_ERROR naming the fields it does honour, and a missing query in search mode is CONFIG_ERROR — never a silent help fallback. Runs an in-memory body index (articles and account-wide assets) unioned with Hudu's own text search, so a record written a second ago still surfaces. The index is built from list pages: no per-record fetch is issued. With a cold index this answers from Hudu's search alone and reports degraded body-not-indexed, because Hudu never matches article body content. limit defaults to 8 and is hard-capped at 25 (a larger value throws CONFIG_ERROR, never a silent clamp); scope defaults to articles and assets. Each hit carries a snippet (a verbatim slice of the stripped text) and a fetch call for the full record. Every bound that bites is named in the response reasons list with complete false, and one resource failing becomes a failure entry instead of losing the call. The scoreScope field says whether the scores are comparable across resources.","compact":"KnowledgeSearchResult"},
